        # contains full vec16/vec8/vec4/scalar stride loops, but the old launch
        # sized the grid so each thread did exactly one 16-element chunk,
        # creating 131072 tiny blocks. Block churn on this DRAM-bound kernel
        # matches the profiler's occupancy gap (79.7% achieved vs 100%
        # theoretical). Launching exactly one full wave of persistent CTAs
        # (SMs * max resident blocks) keeps every warp slot filled while the
        # kernel's existing stride loop covers all chunks, preserving exact
        # semantics and tail handling for any n.
